course: dictionary
lesson: 9085
title: Slower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slower means moving or working with less speed, or taking more time to do something. It is the comparing form of slow: slow, slower, slowest. We use slower when we compare two things, as in «The snail is slower than the ant.»
explain: Slower can also be about time. «A clock that is slower shows an earlier time than the real time.» So a slower clock is behind the real time. Look at the words around slower to find out which meaning it has, because they are its context.
explain: «Herring gulls learn that people carry food and swoop to grab it; scientists in England found gulls were slower to grab food when a person stared straight at them.» Here slower means took longer to act. Check by swapping in your meaning: "took longer to grab food" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Slow is the basic word, slower is the comparing word, and slowest is used for three or more things.
fact: «Slower» means with less speed, or taking more time to do something.
fact: A clock that is slower shows an earlier time than the real time.
fact: A bus going 40 km/h is 10 km/h slower than a car going 50 km/h, because 50 − 10 = 40.
fact: Things slow down because of friction, a force that rubs against movement.
exercise: «The snail is slower than the ant.» What does slower mean here? | Faster and louder | *With less speed | Taller and brighter | Happier and kinder
exercise: A car goes 50 km/h. A bus is 10 km/h slower than the car. What speed is the bus? | 10 km/h | 50 km/h | *40 km/h | 60 km/h
exercise: «Our clock is slower than the real time.» Which time does the clock show? | The same time exactly | *An earlier time | A later time | Midnight, always
test: Why should drivers slow down near schools? | So the car stops working | *So they move with less speed where children may be | To drive faster past the school gate | So the car can get louder
test: Which word is the comparing form of slow? | *slower | slowest | slowly | slowness
exam: «Gulls were slower to grab food when a person stared at them.» What does slower mean here? | Ate more food | Flew faster | Stopped for ever | *Took more time to act
